r over two hours while workers prepared the course. One of the favorites, " [:a {:href "/athletes/86083"} "Marc Girardelli"] ", was the first off in the downhill and crashed wildly early on, taking him out of the competition. The 1991-92 World Cup leader was " [:a {:href "/athletes/83156"} "Paul Accola"] ", who skied cautiously to finish the downhill in fifth place. On the first run of the slalom, Accola missed a gate early, climbing back up the course, he managed to finish but was a full 8 seconds behind the slalom first run leader, 1988 combined gold medalist, " [:a {:href "/athletes/97903"} "Hubert Strolz"] " of Austria. Strolz was leading going into the second run, and looked set to defend his gold medal. But near the finish of run two, he missed a gate and was disqualified. Amidst this carnage, the gold medal would go to the virtually unknown Italian " [:a {:href "/athletes/96516"} "Josef Polig"] ", with the silver won by his even less-well-known teammate, " [:a {:href "/athletes/92168"} "Gianfranco Martin"] "."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Points"] [:th {} "Downhill"] [:th {} "Slalom"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "29"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/96516"} "Josef Polig"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/ITA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/ITA.png"}] "ITA"]] [:td {} "14.58"] [:td {} "1:45.78 (6)"] [:td {} "1:42.16 (5)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {:class "bib"} "21"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/92168"} "Gianfranco Martin"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/ITA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/ITA.png"}] "ITA"]] [:td {} "14.90